button, not to mention ì people who record shows to omit commer¬ 
cials altogether. Not every ş guilty, though. House, on Fox, is still 
four acts (plus a teaser) for example. But elsewhere, potentially interesting 
shows such as Nip/Tuck (on FX) are so chopped up the ³ begins to 
feel like decoration between the ads. 
Like it or not, ű to find out if · you’re speculating has 
four, five, six or even seven acts, and ø re-configure your structure, 
f suggest you begin µ four-act idea. Then take what used to be 
the teaser and lengthen it to around ten pages to create a new Act One. 
