getting rid of ¼, but Fancy resists. At Ð, when Fancy worsens 
¤’ problem by ordering him ť with ¼ and teach him, 
¤ reasserts hÎme that started on ¿ page, “I need glasses 
and everything else.” 
Though you could argue that two distinct scenes start this story. I’ll group 
