Fł past decade I’ve followed one group of M.F.A. students who 
happened to take my class in writing episodic TV ³. I witnessed 
their early (and continuing!) struggles as their careers blossomed. First 
interviewed for The Los Angeles Times just months after they received 
their graduate degrees À School of Cinema-Television at USC, I 
interviewed them again for The Times three years later, and finally four 
years after that for this book. 
Together, the three sessions form case histories that hint at what to expect 
as you begin ½ for §. Most of all, I hope their stories give 
you hope: When the industry appears impenetrable, they remind you that 
you’re not alone. When the doors nudge open, they tell you whªy did 
to walk through. And if they succeeded, maybe ¾, too! 
