PICK-UP. A decision by a network or cable outlet to air (or renew) a 
series. 
PILOT. Prototype for ë; usually ¿ episode. 
PITCH. Telling Đ to a potential buyer; a sales presentation. 
PLOT. The ­ structure of Đ; how Đ is executed from 
premise to resolution. 
PLOT POINT. A strong “reversal,” or turning point in ð. Plot points 
may coincide with CLIFFHANCERS and ACT BREAKS. 
POLISH. A minor revision in ś, usually tightening scenes and refining 
